# Everything in this repo runs on Linux. A file committed with CRLF endings
# breaks at runtime, not at review time: bash fails on a CRLF shebang with
# "$'\r': command not found", which would take out install-sentinel.sh for
# every user, and python3 chokes the same way on a CRLF script.
#
# Forcing LF in the index *and* the working tree means a contributor on
# Windows cannot accidentally publish CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
